    {
      "id": "s05",
      "type": "APPLE_STAGE",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "So why is open ear the hard version? A sealed tip blocks sound with rubber, physically, before any chip is involved. An open bud has no seal at all, which means every decibel you don't hear was cancelled by computation instead.",
      "data": {
        "appleStage": {
          "headline": "No seal means [no head start]",
          "kind": "compare-bars",
          "caption": "Where the quiet comes from",
          "premise": "Apple's own relative figure: AirPods 4 as the baseline, AirPods 5 against it.",
          "color": "purple",
          "cells": [
            {
              "label": "AirPods 5",
              "text": "bar",
              "sub": "up to 1.5x more ANC",
              "value": 150,
              "atWord": 7.917
            },
            {
              "label": "AirPods 4",
              "text": "bar",
              "sub": "the baseline",
              "value": 100,
              "atWord": 3.75
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 434,
      "audio": "audio/apple-airpods_long_s05.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "type": "APPLE_STAGE",
      "transition": "iris",
      "background": "zoneC",
      "narration": "What does the listening, though? Two beamforming microphones face outwards — beamforming just means the pair work out which direction a sound came from. A third microphone points inwards, into your ear, checking what actually got through. An optical sensor knows when the bud is in. And a second accelerometer feels your jaw move as you talk, so the H2 chip can tell your voice from everybody else's in a noisy room.",
      "data": {
        "appleStage": {
          "headline": "Five sensors, [one H2 chip]",
          "kind": "airpods",
          "caption": "What the H2 chip hears",
          "premise": "Dual beamforming mics, an inward mic, an optical sensor and two accelerometers.",
          "color": "green",
          "cells": [
            {
              "label": "Two beamforming mics",
              "text": "stem",
              "sub": "they hear direction",
              "atWord": 5.5
            },
            {
              "label": "Inward-facing mic",
              "text": "bud",
              "sub": "checks what got through",
              "atWord": 26.083
            },
            {
              "label": "Optical in-ear sensor",
              "text": "bud",
              "sub": "knows when you wear it",
              "atWord": 28.333
            },
            {
              "label": "Speech accelerometer",
              "text": "stem",
              "sub": "feels your jaw move",
              "atWord": 41.5
