    {
      "id": "s07",
      "type": "APPLE_STAGE",
      "transition": "slide",
      "background": "zoneC",
      "narration": "All of that feeds four things you'll use without thinking about them. Transparency lets the room back in, which means you still hear a platform announcement. Adaptive Audio blends the two as your surroundings change, because a train is not a library. Conversation Awareness drops the volume the moment you start talking. And Live Translation runs hands-free, so a language you don't speak arrives in your ear while the other person is still saying it, without you touching anything at all.",
      "data": {
        "appleStage": {
          "headline": "Four modes, [no menu]",
          "kind": "airpods",
          "caption": "Transparency, Adaptive, Awareness, Translation",
          "premise": "Four listening behaviours on one pair of buds, switched by the chip, not by you.",
          "color": "blue",
