      "type": "APPLE_STAGE",
      "transition": "whippan",
      "background": "zoneC",
      "narration": "The controls all sit on the stem, and they're worth learning, because the alternative is digging your phone out. Press once to play or pause, twice to skip forward, three times to go back, and press and hold to switch listening modes. Then there's the one that isn't on both models: on the higher-priced pair you swipe up or down the stem to change the volume, which sounds minor until you've spent a month reaching into a pocket to turn something down.",
